2. Method reference implementations
===============================================================================

The codebase of Zheng et al. re-implements several continual learning methods
for language models. As stated in its source files, parts of these
implementations follow the official code of the respective methods. The
corresponding files of this repository carry the same references in their
headers.

  DER++   Buzzega et al., Dark Experience for General Continual Learning:
          a Strong, Simple Baseline. NeurIPS 2020.
          https://github.com/aimagelab/mammoth
          MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Pietro Buzzega, Matteo Boschini,
          Angelo Porrello, Davide Abati, Simone Calderara
          -> models/DERpp.py

  CLS-ER  Arani et al., Learning Fast, Learning Slow: A General Continual
          Learning Method based on Complementary Learning System. ICLR 2022.
          https://github.com/NeurAI-Lab/CLS-ER (built on mammoth)
          MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Pietro Buzzega, Matteo Boschini,
          Angelo Porrello, Davide Abati, Simone Calderara
          -> models/CLSER.py (EMA updates of the plastic and stable models)

  LAMOL   Sun et al., LAMOL: LAnguage MOdeling for Lifelong Language
          Learning. ICLR 2020.
          https://github.com/jojotenya/LAMOL
          MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 jojotenya, Copyright (c) 2020 Daikon-Sun
          -> models/LAMOL.py, models/LAMOL_KD.py, models/L2KD.py,
             utils/dataloader.py (pseudo-sample generation and data format)

  L2KD    Chuang et al., Lifelong Language Knowledge Distillation.
          EMNLP 2020.
          https://github.com/voidism/L2KD (builds on LAMOL; no license stated)
          -> models/L2KD.py (word-level distillation)

  PCLL    Zhao et al., Prompt Conditioned VAE: Enhancing Generative Replay
          for Lifelong Learning in Task-Oriented Dialogue. EMNLP 2022.
          https://github.com/AlibabaResearch/DAMO-ConvAI/tree/main/pcll
          MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Alibaba Research
          -> models/PCLL.py, utils/dataloader.py

  VAG     Shao et al., Class-Incremental Learning based on Label
          Generation. ACL 2023.
          https://github.com/shaoyijia/VAG (no license stated)
          -> utils/dataformat_preprocess.py (FewRel/TACRED label mapping)

